      'Euless shares its eastern edge with DFW International, and the businesses along SH 360 and the airport frontage, from parking operations to crew hotels and freight yards, keep their gates running around the clock. DoorKing equipment on entrances like these carries two kinds of load. The operator cycles hundreds of times a day, so gearbox wear and chain and track wear arrive early. The access side is just as busy: card readers and keypads handle shift changes at all hours, and when a shift pattern changes, the programming has to follow. A gate that refuses certain staff at five in the morning is often an access schedule problem, not a broken operator.',
