      'HySecurity operators are engineered for continuous, high-cycle duty on secure commercial and industrial sites, and that is exactly the use they get along the airport side of Euless. A hydraulic SlideDriver on a logistics yard or parking entrance may cycle hundreds of times a day, every day. That workload brings its own failures: hydraulic pressure loss and seal wear, Smart Touch controller faults with error codes on the display, drive belt or chain wear, encoder and limit drift, and loop detector and safety device faults in lanes crossed by heavy vehicles. Pump and motor wear accumulates where a site never pauses.',
      'Most HySecurity faults are repairable. A SlideDriver or SlideDriver II with low pressure usually needs seals and a pressure check, while a controller fault is traced from its error code before any part is ordered. Track and drive wear is assessed at the same time, because on a gate that never stops, every part ages together. Sites off SH 360 and Industrial Boulevard are in our service area.',
